// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-034
=adr: 034
=title: Stale Derived State Display When Workflow Is Deleted
=date: 2026-02-26
=status: accepted

#ctx
~problem: workflow deletion leaves device_derived_states intact (ADR-032 Level3); dashboard gauges silently show stale workflow-computed values with no indication producing workflow is gone
~risk: industrial IoT operators may trust stale values as live → safety concern

#decision
=model_change: DeviceDerivedState gains stale:Boolean(default=false) + staledAt:Date(default=null)
=service_upsert: upsert() resets stale=false + staledAt=null on every write (workflow alive)
=service_mark_stale: markAllStale() → sets stale=true + staledAt=now on ALL device_derived_states
=workflow_delete: WorkflowService.delete() calls deviceDerivedStateService.markAllStale() after deletion
~circular_dep: dynamic import used in workflow.service.ts to avoid circular dependency
=api_response: GET /devices/:deviceId now returns derivedStateMeta:{stale,staledAt} alongside derivedState

=frontend_hook: useDeviceRealtime() return_type changed to { state:DeviceState|null, stale:boolean, staledAt:string|null }
=staleMeta: seeded from device.derivedStateMeta on HTTP fetch; cleared on WS derived event
=gauge_ui: {
  ring: ring-2 ring-amber-400 dark:ring-amber-500 when stale=true,
  badge: 'Stale' pill top-right with amber indicator dot,
  tooltip: "Workflow deleted — showing last known value as of {staledAt}"
}
!breaking_change: useDeviceRealtime callers MUST destructure {state,stale,staledAt}
~only_caller: RealTimeGaugeBlock (already updated)
!no_data_loss: device_derived_states retained per ADR-032 Level3

#consequences
+pos: [operators_informed_value_not_live, no_data_loss, auto_recovery_on_workflow_restart]
-neg: [markAllStale_is_org_agnostic→all_devices_marked_stale_on_any_workflow_delete]
~future: per-org markAllStale when multi-org is fully enforced

#scope
=arch_summary_update: yes
